      "commitMessage": "fix(nightly): pull affiliate revenue BEFORE the collectors read it\n\nOrdering bug found by running it. collectors/amazon.ts reads\ndata/affiliate/latest.json, but the pull was sitting in the L2 probe\nblock — after collect:all. So the collector reported on the PREVIOUS\nnight's snapshot every night, permanently one day stale.\n\nThe first live run showed the sharp version: the collector logged\n\"latest.json does not exist yet — the automated pull has not run\nsuccessfully\" while the pull wrote that exact file minutes later in the\nsame job.\n\nMoved chromium install + the affiliate pull ahead of the collectors. The\npull is data acquisition, not a probe; it only sat with the probes\nbecause that is where chromium happened to be installed. Both steps now\nshare the one install, so this costs nothing."
